{
  "case_id": "2008-07-984",
  "document_hash": "5fe0ab4dec86271b1d1d08faede5b3efe9e946617cf8d16cc6b7e27ed4e3bae2",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-984",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5fe0ab4dec86271b1d1d08faede5b3efe9e946617cf8d16cc6b7e27ed4e3bae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5fe0ab4dec86-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We will hear argument first this morning in Case 07-984, Coeur Alaska v. The Southeast Alaska Conservation Council, and Case 07-990, Alaska v. The Southeast Alaska Conservation Council."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2008-07-984",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5fe0ab4dec86271b1d1d08faede5b3efe9e946617cf8d16cc6b7e27ed4e3bae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5fe0ab4dec86-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The expert agencies charged by Congress with implementing the Clean Water Act have concluded that the discharge of fill material, like the mine tailings at issue in this case, should be permitted by the Army Corps of Engineers under section 404 of the Act, and are not -- are not subject to the effluent guidelines applicable to permits issued by the EPA under section 402 of the Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-984",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5fe0ab4dec86271b1d1d08faede5b3efe9e946617cf8d16cc6b7e27ed4e3bae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5fe0ab4dec86-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If the discharge comes from a single pipe, is it always one or the other, or can it ever be both fill and --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-984",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5fe0ab4dec86271b1d1d08faede5b3efe9e946617cf8d16cc6b7e27ed4e3bae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5fe0ab4dec86-0001-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The definition that was adopted, if I have it right, was the EPA definition."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson (Government)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-984",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5fe0ab4dec86271b1d1d08faede5b3efe9e946617cf8d16cc6b7e27ed4e3bae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5fe0ab4dec86-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If it's fill, the administrating, permitting agency is the Army Corps of Engineers."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-984",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5fe0ab4dec86271b1d1d08faede5b3efe9e946617cf8d16cc6b7e27ed4e3bae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5fe0ab4dec86-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But it can contain it so long as it is -- as it -- as it is not transitory."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-984",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5fe0ab4dec86271b1d1d08faede5b3efe9e946617cf8d16cc6b7e27ed4e3bae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5fe0ab4dec86-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "My question is, does it apply to solids?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Waldo (Respondents)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-984",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5fe0ab4dec86271b1d1d08faede5b3efe9e946617cf8d16cc6b7e27ed4e3bae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5fe0ab4dec86-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "EPA has always regulated industrial sources that -- whose raw processed wastewater contains high levels of suspended solids, high enough that it would have the effect of fill material and can be considered fill."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-984",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5fe0ab4dec86271b1d1d08faede5b3efe9e946617cf8d16cc6b7e27ed4e3bae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5fe0ab4dec86-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: To fill material as defined in the 2002 regulation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-984",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5fe0ab4dec86271b1d1d08faede5b3efe9e946617cf8d16cc6b7e27ed4e3bae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5fe0ab4dec86-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Well, if it really felt that way, couldn't it simply have vetoed the permit?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-984",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5fe0ab4dec86271b1d1d08faede5b3efe9e946617cf8d16cc6b7e27ed4e3bae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5fe0ab4dec86-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Is it right -- now, I am back on my hobby horse -- but is it right that this slurry is pushing into this lake 50 feet or 75 feet covering the bottom with some stuff? A lot of it's dirt, and some of it's the worst chemical ever, except"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2008-07-984",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5fe0ab4dec86271b1d1d08faede5b3efe9e946617cf8d16cc6b7e27ed4e3bae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5fe0ab4dec86-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There is a 402 permit in this case, too there is a 404 permit with respect to material going into the lake and a 402 permit for the material coming out of the lake into the waters of the United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2008-07-984",
